# The NON-UNIFORM loft (#210, on #207's fix): the corpus's minimal
# pair with `loft_prism`. The SAME three sections -- squares [-1,1]^2
# at the ends, the non-affine trapezoid (-1.375,-1)(1.375,-1)(1,1)
# (-1,1) in the middle -- at the SAME v-degree 2, moved from z = 0,1,2
# to z = 0,1,**3**. Section spacing 1 : 2 instead of 1 : 1 is the whole
# difference, and until #207 it was the difference between a body and a
# refusal: the skin fit synthesized a weight channel whose LU
# round-trip landed an ulp off 1.0 on exactly this parameterization,
# making every wall bitwise RATIONAL, poisoning `speed_lower_bound`,
# and refusing the body at assembly.
#
# Census 6/12/8 is `loft_prism`'s (same topology, different placement):
# 2 planar caps + 4 non-rational B_SPLINE_SURFACE_WITH_KNOTS walls;
# 8 exact line rims + 4 NURBS wall-wall seams; 4+4 corners. OCC keeps
# it -- open (non-closed) B-spline patches import without added seam or
# degenerate edges.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- V
#
# EXACT ANALYTIC, in FreeCAD's internal mm³, not a readback.
#
# (1) The v-parameterization. `sweep::loft_parameters` averages the
#     normalized cumulative CHORD lengths over every control row of
#     every wall -- each corner twice, as two walls' row. The two
#     flared bottom corners, (-1,-1,z) <-> (-1.375,-1,z) and
#     (1,-1,z) <-> (1.375,-1,z), travel
#       √(0.375² + 1²) = √73/8   and
#       √(0.375² + 2²) = √265/8,
#     the two top corners 1 and 2, so the middle parameter is
#       t = (√73 / (√73 + √265) + 1/3) / 2 = 0.33876641703757304,
#     NOT the 1/3 that the z-spacing alone would suggest -- the flare
#     lengthens the first chord. (Compare `loft_prism`, where the
#     symmetric spacing forces t = 1/2 whatever the flare does.)
#
# (2) The fit. Three sections at degree 2 give the clamped knot vector
#     [0,0,0,1,1,1]: one Bezier span, so each corner path is the unique
#     QUADRATIC through its three section points at parameters
#     [0, t, 1] -- the Lagrange interpolant, with
#       L1(v) = v(v-1) / (t(t-1)),   L2(v) = v(v-t) / (1-t).
#
# (3) The slices. All four corners share one z-channel, so every fixed-v
#     slice is planar: z(v) = L1(v) + 3*L2(v), monotone on [0,1]
#     (z' runs 2.856 -> 3.144). The x-channel is the end value plus
#     d*L1(v) at the two flaring bottom corners (d = 0.375) and constant
#     at the two top ones; walls are degree 1 in u, so the slice is the
#     straight-edged trapezoid of area A(v) = 4 + 2*d*L1(v).
#
# (4) The integral. V = int_0^1 A(v) z'(v) dv = 4*(z(1)-z(0)) + 2d*I
#     with I = int_0^1 L1 z' dv. Writing z' = L1' + 3 L2', the first
#     term dies exactly: int_0^1 (v^2-v)(2v-1) dv = 0. The second gives
#     int_0^1 (v^2-v)(2v-t) dv = (t-1)/6, so I = 1/(2 t (1-t)), and
#       V = 12 + 0.375 / (t(1-t))
#         = 12 + 13.5 (a+b)^2 / ((4a+b)(2a+5b))   [a = √73, b = √265]
#         = 13.674079253555504 m³ = 13674079253.555504 mm³.
#
# The kernel's certified midpoint below is 13674079253.555506 -- ONE
# ulp away (1.91e-6 mm³), which is 5.39e-2 of the certified pad: the
# analytic value sits inside the certified enclosure with 18.5x margin
# -- comfortably, but not by decades. RTOL stays at the 1e-9 default:
# these walls are piecewise-POLYNOMIAL ruled patches (degree 1x2), well
# inside GProp's Gauss order, exactly as for `loft_prism` (local FreeCAD
# read this fixture back at its analytic value to 13 digits at its
# previous parameterization, on walls of the same degrees).
#
# KERNEL_* pin the NATIVE body's census and certified volume, full
# precision (the literal is the export writer's round-tripping float
# printer's output; crates/step-export/tests/kernel_sidecars.rs asserts
# these lines against the live kernel). scripts/check_step.sh consumes
# EXPECT_* (what FreeCAD/OCC reports after import) and ignores KERNEL_*.
# The certified volume is a QUADRATURE enclosure (the NURBS walls have
# no closed form): midpoint ± pad, both FUNCTIONS of ambient ε,
# pinned at the corpus's declared uncertainty ε = 1e-9 -- which is why
# the staleness row byte-pins the pair only at ε = 1e-9 and asserts
# enclosure overlap at other ε.
KERNEL_SOLIDS=1
KERNEL_SHELLS=1
KERNEL_FACES=6
KERNEL_EDGES=12
KERNEL_VERTICES=8
KERNEL_VOLUME_MM3=13674079253.555506
KERNEL_VOLUME_PAD_MM3=3.5379107051388324E-5
EXPECT_SOLIDS=1
EXPECT_SHELLS=1
EXPECT_FACES=6
EXPECT_EDGES=12
EXPECT_VERTICES=8
EXPECT_VOLUME_MM3=13674079253.555504
